WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:14.743
The dead tiger lay at Mowgli's feet.

2
00:00:14.763 --> 00:00:20.267
"We must work fast," Mowgli said to Akela and Gray Brother.

3
00:00:20.287 --> 00:00:24.229
"I want to lay the tiger's hide at Council Rock."

4
00:00:27.151 --> 00:00:29.192
They got to work preparing the hide.

5
00:00:30.056 --> 00:00:35.418
Suddenly the wolves dashed off, and Mowgli felt a hand clamp down on his shoulder.

6
00:00:36.518 --> 00:00:38.578
Buldeo stood there with his gun.

7
00:00:40.179 --> 00:00:42.680
"That tiger's hide belongs to me!"

8
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.380
the hunter growled.

9
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.281
"There's a big reward for it."

10
00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.701
Mowgli rolled his eyes.

11
00:00:49.721 --> 00:00:54.363
"I'm sure you're planning to give me some of the reward."

12
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:58.464
"I'm the chief hunter," Buldeo said.

13
00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.641
"I'm not going to give you any of the reward.

14
00:01:02.722 --> 00:01:05.783
You caught the tiger only because of dumb luck."

15
00:01:07.464 --> 00:01:11.105
He stooped over Shere Khan, looking at the tiger closely.

16
00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:16.167
"This tiger and I are old enemies," Mowgli said.

17
00:01:17.068 --> 00:01:18.448
Then he waved an arm.

18
00:01:18.468 --> 00:01:26.592
"Akela!" Seconds later Buldeo found himself lying on the grass.

19
00:01:27.452 --> 00:01:29.693
A large gray wolf stood over him.

20
00:01:30.394 --> 00:01:32.295
Buldeo blinked in surprise.

21
00:01:33.055 --> 00:01:34.836
Mowgli had summoned a wolf!

22
00:01:34.856 --> 00:01:38.378
"This is magic of the worst kind!"

23
00:01:38.818 --> 00:01:39.339
he thought.

24
00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:43.041
Terrified, he lay as still as a stone.

25
00:01:43.721 --> 00:01:45.782
What if Mowgli summoned more wolves?

26
00:01:46.262 --> 00:01:49.324
Or he turned himself into a wolf or tiger?

27
00:01:49.344 --> 00:01:53.606
"Great King," Buldeo said at last in a whisper.

28
00:01:53.626 --> 00:01:56.588
"Yes?" Mowgli grinned.

29
00:01:57.808 --> 00:01:59.849
Now the hunter was afraid of him.

30
00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:01.829
"I'm an old man.

31
00:02:02.429 --> 00:02:05.030
I didn't know that you were a powerful sorcerer.

32
00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:06.550
May I get up?

33
00:02:07.171 --> 00:02:09.171
Will your wolf tear me to pieces?"

34
00:02:09.191 --> 00:02:17.133
"Go. But from now on, leave me alone," Mowgli replied.

35
00:02:17.153 --> 00:02:20.714
"Let him go, Akela," he commanded.

36
00:02:24.175 --> 00:02:27.316
Buldeo limped away to the village as fast as he could.

37
00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:31.629
Every few minutes he looked back nervously.

38
00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:38.612
When he got to the village, he told the villagers about what he'd seen.

39
00:02:41.273 --> 00:02:44.415
Mowgli and the others finished preparing the tiger's hide.

40
00:02:46.836 --> 00:02:48.476
Mowgli hid it near a tree.

41
00:02:50.997 --> 00:02:54.999
Then he gathered the buffalo herd and took them back to the village.

42
00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:59.532
As he approached, bells clanged loudly.

43
00:03:00.473 --> 00:03:03.494
Half the village seemed to be waiting for him by the gate.

44
00:03:03.514 --> 00:03:10.375
"The villagers are happy that I killed the tiger," Mowgli said to himself proudly.

45
00:03:10.395 --> 00:03:13.176
"They must be waiting to thank me!"

46
00:03:16.737 --> 00:03:21.178
Instead a shower of stones whistled past Mowgli's ears.

47
00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:23.379
Angry shouts rose.

48
00:03:23.399 --> 00:03:27.320
"Sorcerer!" "Jungle demon!"

49
00:03:28.116 --> 00:03:29.336
"Shoot him, Buldeo!"

50
00:03:30.557 --> 00:03:32.757
The old gun went off with a bang.

51
00:03:33.778 --> 00:03:37.179
But the bullet missed Mowgli—striking a buffalo instead.

52
00:03:37.199 --> 00:03:40.660
"The boy just used magic again!"

53
00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.020
a villager shouted.

54
00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.081
"He turned that bullet around with magic!"

55
00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:48.482
The villagers threw more stones at Mowgli.

56
00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.503
He ducked, trying not to panic.

57
00:03:52.623 --> 00:03:55.384
Akela and Gray Brother ran to his sides.

58
00:03:56.532 --> 00:03:59.615
"This is just like the wolf pack," Akela said.

59
00:03:59.635 --> 00:04:02.518
"They want you gone, Mowgli."

60
00:04:03.859 --> 00:04:07.222
"Last time I was told to leave because I'm a human."

61
00:04:09.223 --> 00:04:10.104
Mowgli sighed.

62
00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:13.287
"This time it is because I am a wolf!"

63
00:04:14.808 --> 00:04:17.611
Just then Messua ran out from the crowd.

64
00:04:17.631 --> 00:04:20.173
"My son!

65
00:04:20.753 --> 00:04:23.256
Are the stories about your magic true?"

66
00:04:25.128 --> 00:04:28.049
Mowgli ducked as more stones whizzed by his head.

67
00:04:28.069 --> 00:04:30.990
"I'm not a sorcerer, Messua.

68
00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.530
You know that."

69
00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.311
"You must go away before they hurt you!"

70
00:04:36.871 --> 00:04:37.352
she said.

71
00:04:38.412 --> 00:04:40.933
A few people pumped their fists in the air.

72
00:04:40.953 --> 00:04:43.774
"Get away from the sorcerer, Messua!"

73
00:04:44.014 --> 00:04:44.694
they shouted.

74
00:04:44.714 --> 00:04:47.995
"Come back here, or we will stone you too!"

75
00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:53.132
Mowgli quickly hugged Messua.

76
00:04:53.152 --> 00:04:55.273
He thanked her for her kindness to him.

77
00:04:56.194 --> 00:05:00.597
Then he and the two wolves ran away from the people's village.
